    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here's what happens on `POST /api/owners`, in order.\n\n## Gate (whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`; without that role the request is denied before any step runs.\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step below carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads/writes run in one transaction that commits once at the end (or rolls back if any step throws).\n\n## Step-by-step (the 13-step pipeline in `owners.POST.yml`)\n\n**1. `ValidateNewOwner`** \u2014 reads the body once (`@RequestBody`), and in this order:\n- Normalizes `address` (trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) and **writes it back onto the request**.\n- Required-field check on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (blank-tested *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` \u2192 any missing/blank throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**, lists offending fields).\n- Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 and **writes it back**; unformable / wrong national length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n- Normalizes `email` (trim, lower-case, syntax-checked) and **writes it back**; blank \u2192 left unset; invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**).\n- Validates optional `postcode` (must be 4 digits, and within the city's region range NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099; unknown region accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). Absent postcode is accepted.\n- Publishes the normalized request for later steps.\n\n**2. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 builds an identity key (`normalizedTelephone | email | would-be householdId`) and scans all existing owners; an exact whole-key match \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n**3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); \u2265 50 \u2192 `OwnerCityFullException` (**409**).\n\n**4. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 takes the effective registration date (request value, else today), rolls it forward to a business day, and counts existing owners stamped with that day; \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**5. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent; **rolls weekend dates forward to the next Monday**; publishes the entity.\n\n**6. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `NNNN` is (count of owners already in that city) + 1, zero-padded.\n\n**7. `AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (last two digits of the registration year).\n\n**8. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 only if the request has `sharesHousehold = true` **and** an existing owner shares the same last name + normalized address: assigns the shared `householdId` to the new owner **and writes it back onto (and saves) each existing same-household owner** that doesn't already carry it. Otherwise leaves `householdId` unset. *(This is the one step that mutates and persists other records.)*\n\n**9. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first + last name (case-insensitive), counted before this owner is saved.\n\n**10. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the new owner (assigns its id).\n\n**11. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line: `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and derived `membershipLevel` (base 1, +1 if email present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3).\n\n**12. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when **more than 80** owners share the owner's registration day), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Validations (fail-fast, in order):** required fields (400) \u2192 telephone E.164 (400) \u2192 email syntax (400) \u2192 postcode/region (400) \u2192 identity-key uniqueness (409) \u2192 city capacity \u226550 (409) \u2192 daily limit \u2265100 (429).\n- **Side-effects (in order):** mutates the request DTO (address/telephone/email normalized) \u2192 builds entity with business-day registration date \u2192 stamps customerCode, membershipNumber, householdId, namesakeCount \u2192 **saves existing same-household owners** \u2192 saves the new owner \u2192 writes an AUDIT log line \u2192 returns 201 with a `bulkSignupWarning` flag and `Location` header.\n\nNote the validations run **first-to-last with fail-fast ordering deliberately chosen** (e.g. body validation before uniqueness so a bad body is a 400, not masked by a 409), and because governance spans the whole pipeline, an escalation at any step rolls back the household write-backs and the new-owner insert together."
